  "tagline": "Lightweight embedded object database for Java (and .NET) that stores plain objects in one file; dormant.",
  "description": "NeoDatis ODB is a small open-source object database that persists Java objects as they are, with no mapping files, annotations or base classes, into a single database file; ports existed for .NET, and it ran on Android, Groovy and Scala. It offered ACID transactions, indexes, criteria and native queries, a client/server mode and a GUI object explorer, and around 2008–2011 it was a common lightweight alternative to db4o in desktop and Android apps. The 1.9 line was last updated in November 2010 and a 2.x beta never reached a final release; the project is effectively abandoned, though its website still says otherwise. Its .NET port lived on briefly as NDatabase.",
